ute_reply":"2026-09-13T12:18:09.351912Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"retention (n=200, short mode, origin provenance):\n keep_ratio      policy   gold  distractor  question  system  prompt_all\n       0.25   attention 0.0915      0.3052    0.9752  0.0471      0.2459\n       0.25      random 0.2303      0.2251    0.2235  0.2338      0.2278\n       0.25     recency 0.0448      0.3308    1.0000  0.0000      0.2402\n       0.25 sink_recent 0.0454      0.3295    1.0000  0.0172      0.2450\n       0.50   attention 0.2944      0.6067    0.9916  0.2064      0.4958\n       0.50      random 0.4964      0.4946    0.4920  0.4945      0.4951\n       0.50     recency 0.1280      0.7274    1.0000  0.0000      0.4913\n       0.50 sink_recent 0.1286      0.7241    1.0000  0.0172      0.4949\n\nquestion-span retention vs quality, the load-bearing pair:\n   mode  keep_ratio      policy  question  gold    em  decode_p50\nexplain        0.25   attention     0.975 0.092 0.063        92.0\nexplain        0.25      random     0.224 0.230 0.004       256.0\nexplain        0.25     recency     1.000 0.045 0.000        85.5\nexplain        0.25 sink_recent     1.000 0.045 0.031       104.0\nexplain        0.50   attention     0.992 0.294 0.040        86.0\nexplain        0.50      random     0.492 0.496 0.126       121.0\nexplain        0.50     recency     1.000 0.128 0.002       256.0\nexplain        0.50 sink_recent     1.000 0.129 0.058       108.0\n  short        0.25   attention     0.975 0.092 0.299         3.0\n  short        0.25      random     0.224 0.230 0.087        22.0\n  short        0.25     recency     1.000 0.045 0.121         2.0\n  short        0.25 sink_recent     1.000 0.045 0.248         3.0\n  short        0.50   attention     0.992 0.294 0.337         3.0\n  short        0.50      random     0.492 0.496 0.320         3.0\n  short        0.50     recency     1.000 0.128 0.161         2.0\n  short        0.50 sink_recent     1.000 0.129 0.282         3.0\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# notebooks/32_ac_knob4_closeout — CELL 4\n# The knob-4 summary JSON. Structure follows knob 3's: settings, amendments,\n# predictions with outcomes, McNemar dict, and the corrections log.\nPREDICTIONS = {\n    \"efficiency_null\": {\n        \"registered\": \"Eviction imposes a measurable quality cost against an \"\n                      \"efficiency benefit that does not materialise at this \"\n                      \"scale: eviction acts after prefill, peak memory occurs \"\n                      \"during prefill.\",\n        \"outcome\": \"CONFIRMED. Peak memory 6.11-6.15 GiB across all settings \"\n                   \"against 5.87 GiB of weights; evicting 75% of the cache \"\n                   \"moved peak by 0.02 GiB (0.3%). Quality cost is large and \"\n                   \"significant at every setting.\",\n    },\n    \"rope_shift_small\": {\n        \"registered\": \"RoPE position-shifting matters LESS at ~744 tokens than \"\n                      \"in the long-context literature, where holes span \"\n                      \"millions of tokens.\",\n        \"outcome\": \"CONFIRMED in the strongest available form. Paired shifted \"\n                   \"vs naive: b=0 c=0, identical marginals (EM 0.2820 both). \"\n                   \"32/1000 predictions changed, none changed correctness.\",\n    },\n    \"attention_beats_position\": {\n        \"registered\": \"Attention-based eviction beats position-based at equal \"\n                      \"keep_ratio, because gold evidence sits mid-prompt.\",\n        \"outcome\": \"CONFIRMED in short mode at r0.50 and r0.25 (p<0.0001 both), \"\n                   \"null at r0.75 (p=0.1550). Confirmed in explain at r0.25 \"\n                   \"(p=0.0003), null at r0.50 (p=0.0630). But the STATED REASON \"\n                   \"is falsified — see gold_retention below.\",\n    },\n    \"attention_beats_random\": {\n        \"registered\": \"Implied: content-aware selection separates from a coin \"\n                      \"flip.\",\n        \"outcome\": \"BUDGET-DEPENDENT. Short mode: p=0.3317 (r0.75), p=0.1074 \"\n                   \"(r0.50), b=226 c=14 p<0.0001 (r0.25). Initially recorded as \"\n                   \"FALSIFIED from r0.50 alone; the amendment adding r0.75 and \"\n                   \"r0.25 showed the separation exists at tight budgets. A \"\n                   \"single-budget control cannot support a claim about a \"\n                   \"budget-dependent mechanism.\",\n    },\n    \"gold_retention\": {\n        \"registered\": \"Attention wins BECAUSE it retains gold-passage tokens \"\n                      \"better than position policies do.\",\n        \"outcome\": \"FALSIFIED. Gold-span retention, attention vs random: 0.294 \"\n                   \"vs 0.496 (r0.50), 0.091 vs 0.230 (r0.25). Attention retains \"\n                   \"LESS gold and scores HIGHER EM. Rank correlation between \"\n                   \"gold retention and EM flips sign by budget: +0.678 (r0.50), \"\n                   \"-0.581 (r0.25). What predicts quality is retention of the \"\n                   \"QUESTION, not the evidence.\",\n    },\n    \"explain_amplification\": {\n        \"registered\": \"Following knob 3: a longer decode amplifies cache \"\n                      \"damage.\",\n        \"outcome\": \"CONFIRMED at roughly 10x knob 3's magnitude. Paired on the \"\n                   \"307 questions both references answer correctly, \"\n                   \"explain-only-broken vs short-only-broken: 88/0, 168/0, \"\n                   \"60/2, 196/8, 123/0, 174/0, 181/7, 235/2. All p<0.0001.\",\n    },\n}\n\nFINDINGS = [\n    \"Eviction is a large, significant quality cost at every setting, against a \"\n    \"measured efficiency benefit of ~0.3% peak memory. Direct evidence for open \"\n    \"question 1: the long-context KV literature's assumptions do not transfer \"\n    \"to short-context RAG.\",\n    \"What eviction destroys first is the ability to POSE THE TASK, not access \"\n    \"to evidence. At r0.25 all four policies have lost 90-95% of the gold span, \"\n    \"yet short-mode EM ranges 0.087-0.299. Question-span retention separates \"\n    \"them: recency/sink 1.000, attention 0.975, random 0.224.\",\n    \"In explain mode the dominant failure is FORMAT ADHERENCE. Among \"\n    \"generations that stopped cleanly, parse rate is 1.000 at the reference vs \"\n    \"0.058-0.507 under eviction. The model terminates fluently and never emits \"\n    \"the answer marker.\",\n    \"NO POLICY DOMINATES across budget and decode length. Short: attention wins \"\n    \"at r0.25/r0.50, random collapses at r0.25. Explain: attention wins at \"\n    \"r0.25, random wins EM at r0.50 while truncating on 39% of questions vs \"\n    \"attention's 2.5%.\",\n    \"Retrieval rank and eviction survival are COUPLED through prompt position: \"\n    \"gold passages rank early, so position policies cut them first (recency \"\n    \"distractor retention 0.727 vs gold 0.128 at r0.50). A confound absent from \"\n    \"regime 2's pooled corpus, relevant to the Phase 4 knob1 x knob4 surface.\",\n]\n\nCORRECTIONS = [\n    \"rope_scaling is None was the wrong precondition: in transformers 5.0.0 it \"\n    \"aliases rope_parameters, always populated. Correct condition is rope_type \"\n    \"in (default, linear, yarn, llama3), i.e. inv_freq fixed for the run.\",\n    \"Decoded tokens are not a valid instrument for numerical differences on a \"\n    \"random-init model; greedy argmax is near-degenerate there. Logits, and the \"\n    \"direct rotation identity check, are the instruments.\",\n    \"A notebook-23 summary line reported 'eager confound exists: True', \"\n    \"counting a NaN failure as a numerics difference. Two distinct phenomena \"\n    \"conflated.\",\n    \"A full forward materialises logits for every position and OOMs; generate() \"\n    \"slices to the last position. Read hidden states off the base model for \"\n    \"per-row NaN diagnosis.\",\n    \"Three vacuous tests in sequence: comparing `phase` (the packing invariant \"\n    \"forces it identical across layers), asserting on exception TYPE alone \"\n    \"(wrong guard fired), and deriving the stub's inv_freq from the head_dim \"\n    \"under test. Pattern recorded: a guard test must demonstrate the negative \"\n    \"case, not merely go green.\",\n    \"The first verdict helper tested discordant >= 30 before discordant == 0, \"\n    \"printing UNINFORMATIVE for the zero-discordant case the knob-5 amendment \"\n    \"carves out as a NULL.\",\n    \"max_new_tokens=N yields N tokens but N-1 cache appends; endpoints must be \"\n    \"derived from cumulative_length.\",\n    \"evict_sink4_r050 and its naive twin produced identical aggregate EM, b and \"\n    \"c while differing on 32/1000 predictions — a concrete instance of why the \"\n    \"acceptance criterion is paired McNemar and never the aggregate gap.\",\n]\n\nwith open(\"results/knob4_summary.json\", \"w\") as fh:\n    json.dump({\n        \"knob\": 4, \"name\": \"KV cache eviction\", \"regime\": 1,\n        \"n\": 1000, \"reference\": REF, \"batch_size\": 1,\n        \"transformers\": \"5.0.0\",\n        \"policies\": [\"recency\", \"sink_recent\", \"random\", \"attention\"],\n        \"keep_ratios\": {\"short\": [0.75, 0.50, 0.25],\n                        \"explain\": [0.50, 0.25]},\n        \"frozen_constants\": {\"sink\": EV.DEFAULT_SINK, \"seed\": EV.DEFAULT_SEED,\n                             \"shift_rope\": EV.SHIFT_ROPE, \"top_k\": TOP_K},\n        \"arms\": {\n            \"short\": \"results/knob4_short_summary.json\",\n            \"explain\": \"results/knob4_explain_summary.json\",\n            \"retention\": \"results/knob4_retention_summary.json\",\n        },\n        \"predictions\": PREDICTIONS,\n        \"findings\": FINDINGS,\n        \"corrections\": CORRECTIONS,\n        \"settings\": joined.to_dict(\"records\"),\n    }, fh, indent=2, default=str)\nprint(\"wrote results/knob4_summary.json and results/knob4_all_settings.csv\")\nprint(\"COMMIT AND PUSH.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-13T12:18:09.353999Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-13T12:18:09.354258Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-13T12:18:09.37251Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-13T12:18:09.354235Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-13T12:18:09.371432Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"wrote results/knob4_summary.json and results/knob4_all_settings.csv\nCOMMIT AND PUSH.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# notebooks/32_ac_knob4_closeout — CELL 5\n# The retention merge keys on (keep_ratio, policy) only, so EXPLAIN rows\n# inherited SHORT-mode retention from notebook 29 (max_new_tokens=32).\n# Under explain the cache is evicted over ~90 decode steps rather than ~3, so\n# real explain retention is lower. Label the provenance rather than let the\n# numbers read as measured.\njoined = pd.read_csv(\"results/knob4_all_settings.csv\")\nret_cols = [\"gold\", \"distractor\", \"question\", \"system\", \"prompt_all\"]\njoined[\"retention_measured_in\"] = np.where(\n    joined[ret_cols].notna().any(axis=1), \"short\", None)\n\nprint(\"retention provenance by mode:\")\nprint(joined.groupby(\"mode\")[\"retention_measured_in\"]\n      .apply(lambda s: s.notna().sum()).to_string())\nprint(\"\\nEXPLAIN rows carry SHORT-mode retention. Not measured under explain.\")\n\njoined.to_csv(\"results/knob4_all_settings.csv\", index=False)\n\nwith open(\"results/knob4_summary.json\") as fh:\n    S = json.load(fh)\nS[\"caveats\"] = [\n    \"Retention columns (gold/distractor/question/system/prompt_all) were \"\n    \"measured in SHORT mode only (notebook 29, n=200, max_new_tokens=32). \"\n    \"Explain rows inherit them through a (keep_ratio, policy) join and are \"\n    \"NOT measured under explain. Real explain retention is lower: ~90 decode \"\n    \"steps displace more prompt tokens from a fixed budget than ~3 do. The \"\n    \"column retention_measured_in records this.\",\n    \"Retention n=200 (first 200 of the frozen 1000); quality n=1000.\",\n    \"The explain reference evict_none_b1 differs from the frozen explain \"\n    \"baseline on 30/1000 predictions (b=4 c=8 d=12 p=0.3877) — no detectable \"\n    \"EM effect but UNDERPOWERED by the d>=30 rule. The short-mode reference \"\n    \"differed on 2/1000.\",\n]\nS[\"settings\"] = joined.to_dict(\"records\")\nwith open(\"results/knob4_summary.json\", \"w\") as fh:\n    json.dump(S, fh, indent=2, default=str)\nprint(\"\\nupdated results/knob4_summary.json with caveats\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-13T12:24:23.355346Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-13T12:24:23.356167Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-13T12:24:23.37863Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-13T12:24:23.35613Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-13T12:24:23.377606Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"retention provenance by mode:\nmode\nexplain    8\nshort      8\n\nEXPLAIN rows carry SHORT-mode retention. Not measured under explain.\n\nupdated results/knob4_summary.json with caveats\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5}]}